course: dictionary
lesson: 5525
title: Describing things by how they feel
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Leathery means tough, thick and dry, like leather. You can use the words around it to work out its meaning. «Picture a beach after a storm: among the seaweed lies a black leathery pouch with curly corners.» A pouch with curly corners that lies on a beach is not soft or wet like seaweed. It must be tough and dry, so leathery fits.
explain: Leathery can also describe skin. «Leathery skin» is rough and wrinkled, often from lots of sun and wind, so a sailor or farmer who works outdoors may have a leathery face. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence: a tough, dry, wrinkled face still makes sense.
explain: The same word can describe very different things: leaves, eggs, wings and toast. Each time, ask yourself how the thing feels. Cold toast left out too long goes hard and chewy, so it can be leathery too.
fact: Leathery means tough, thick and dry, like leather.
fact: «Leathery» can describe skin that is rough and wrinkled from sun and wind.
fact: Some plants have leathery leaves, such as holly, which helps them save water.
fact: Some turtle and reptile eggs have leathery shells.
fact: Meat cooked for too long can become leathery and hard to chew.
exercise: «Picture a beach after a storm: among the seaweed lies a black leathery pouch with curly corners.» What does leathery mean here? | Soft and wet, like seaweed | Shiny and smooth, like glass | *Tough and dry, like leather | Very loud
exercise: «Leathery skin» is often rough and wrinkled. What is the most likely cause? | Too much sleep | Wearing new shoes | Eating too many sweets | *Lots of sun and wind
exercise: «Some sharks and rays lay eggs in leathery cases called mermaid's purses.» Find and copy the word that tells you what the cases feel like. | rays | *leathery | purses | sharks
test: «Reptiles have dry, scaly skin and most lay eggs with leathery shells.» What does leathery mean here? | Soft and bouncy, like a ball | Cold and wet | Sweet and sticky | *Tough, thick and dry, like leather
test: Toad finds «some fragments of cold and leathery toast». Why would the toast be leathery? | It is still warm and soft | It is made of real leather | *It has gone dry and tough | It has been dipped in honey
exam: Leathery means tough, thick and dry, like what? | Sugar | *Leather | Cotton wool | Water
